# Granot Form Leads Workflow

- `src/parsers/granot/form-leads.ts` parses the Booked Jobs / Follow Up Estimates tables and returns `FollowUpRow` items with `syncable`, `invalid_ref_no`, `unsupported_prior`, or `missing_prior` status. Only `prior` values `1` and `5` are treated as syncable; `0` stays parsed but is not pushed to Vantage.
- `src/parsers/granot/form-edit-lead.ts` parses the current edit page (`ORDREF` + priority level) and also exposes `applyBindingEstimateFeeFromInitialPrice()`, which writes `Binding Estimate Fee` at 85% of the initial price into the first extra-fee fields.
- `scan.ts` sends `PARSE_FOLLOW_UP_ROWS` and returns the parsed response plus the row ids selected by default.
- `preview.ts` resolves each row against Vantage with bounded concurrency. It prefers `GET /api/v1/form-leads/:id`, falls back to `POST /api/v1/form-leads/search` for invalid or missing ids with phone/email, and records `not_found`, `preview_error`, `found_by_fallback`, or `conflict` outcomes without stopping the batch.
- `fallback-resolve.ts` keeps fallback matching deterministic: it flattens server search matches and can auto-resolve a single candidate by matching `ref_no`, Granot source label, or `quoted` alignment with `prior`.
- `payloads.ts` owns the sync predicates and payload shaping. Direct sync only uses rows that are parser-syncable and have `prior` `1` or `5`; fallback sync uses the resolved Vantage `_id`, never the Granot `ref_no`. Duplicate-quarantined form leads are skipped by id.
- `sync.ts` compares the candidate against the current Vantage lead, PATCHes only changed fields, and still sends an idempotent payload when nothing changed so the server can perform its own sync path.
- `cycles.ts` turns parsed rows and row results into the UI-free `CycleDetail` format shared with auto-sync history.
- The tests in `src/test/form-leads-payloads.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-preview-model.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-preview.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-sync.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-fallback-resolve.test.ts`, and `src/test/parsers.test.ts` document the intended fallback, duplicate, and sync behavior.

